    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="0957" n="858" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00 Revolutions/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-17T23:00:00-04:00">February 17, 1936—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 18—12:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. My 16, February 17, 5 p.m. President and most of Cabinet said to be still
                    holding out on gunboat. Revolutionists now claim <pb facs="0958" n="859"
                        xml:id="pg859"/> victory by reason of submission of the loyal forces who
                    have been defending the central section of the city. Latest information seems to
                    confirm this claim. So far as known navy and arsenals still loyal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
